{This combines Parents 0 and 2’s increased H0 weight under relative remaining-work dispersion with Parent 1’s reduction under machine-readiness dispersion. Progress reduces H0’s weight mainly when remaining workloads are similar, retaining its long-work emphasis when they are uneven; readiness dispersion moderates that emphasis without identifying any particular bottleneck machine. These relationships are hypotheses based on H0’s remaining-work reward and H1’s smaller finish-plus-tail preference, requiring external complete-schedule evaluation.}
```python
def use_heuristics(progress, candidate_pair_ratio, remaining_work_mean, remaining_work_std, machine_ready_mean, machine_ready_std, previous_heuristic):
    work_dispersion = remaining_work_std / (remaining_work_mean + remaining_work_std)
    ready_dispersion = machine_ready_std / (machine_ready_mean + machine_ready_std + remaining_work_mean)
    alpha = (
        0.5
        + 0.3 * work_dispersion
        - 0.2 * progress * (1.0 - work_dispersion)
        - 0.1 * ready_dispersion
    )
    return (1, (alpha, 1.0 - alpha, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0))
